# Kconfig for NoMount
#
# Vendored from maxsteeel/nomount kernel/src/.  Upstream declares this as a
# tristate with `default y` so the prebuilt workflows can also build it out
# of tree (=m); in this tree the feature is built-in only (no modules are
# ever shipped), so it is a bool and defaults off - enabled explicitly via
# CONFIG_NOMOUNT=y in the target defconfig.  With or without rules the
# driver registers only a keyring type ("nomount") and touches nothing else
# until a root userspace process submits a payload through add_key(2), so
# leaving it disabled keeps stock behaviour bit for bit.

config NOMOUNT
	bool "NoMount path redirection subsystem (mountless module support)"
	default n
	help
	  NoMount allows path redirection and virtual file injection
	  without mounting filesystems. Useful for systemless modifications.

	  Upstream: https://github.com/maxsteeel/nomount (kernel/src/).
	  Control taps the keyring: a root caller passes a page-pinned
	  "nomount" key payload describing injection/whiteout rules and
	  per-UID exclusions; rules live in RAM and vanish on reboot.
